# -text rather than `text eol=lf`: no conversion in either direction, so a
# checkout can never rewrite bytes whose sha256 is quoted as a certificate.
# These are the mi project's cartridge RunRecords, archived 2026-09-09 so
# that every record sha256 cited in docs/RESEARCH.md and the api-codebase
# wiki resolves to a file in this repository rather than to one
# filesystem's longevity. Cluster-produced records came from
# /pub/wagnera3/mi/cartridge/results/; the sweep-* and
# companions-local-run* records were measured locally on austinpc's
# RTX 3090 Ti (2026-09-04, board a67d6038) and rescued from a
# session-ephemeral scratchpad -- each record's fingerprint names its
# host. Twin/pair files are committed BESIDE their primaries
# deliberately: a byte-identity certificate is verifiable here by
# comparing the two files directly (aa61330b = sweep-v2a/v2b,
# 9e87e816 = companions-local-run1/run2).
cartridge/*.json -text
